TASK 1 COMPLETE — renderer contract repaired, 60 FPS baseline established.

Commit: 6ef1079de
Date: 2026-10-11
Message: B"H Mitzvah World: renderer contract repair + 60fps baseline (Task 1) + blank-meadow instant-start slice (Task 2)

What was done (code-verified, all suites green):
- WebGL capability probe runs BEFORE the essential ledger exists, so the
  first-frame silence clock can never start where no 3D doorway exists.
  Four distinct failure states with precise evidence: WEBGL_UNAVAILABLE,
  RENDERER_INIT_FAILED, ZERO_SIZE_CANVAS, FIRST_FRAME_TIMEOUT.
- Zero-size viewport is its own failure state (no more Math.max(1,...) mask);
  first frame counts only after a REAL render with a nonzero viewport.
- Resize sets BOTH CSS size (viewport px) and backing buffer (viewport x
  capped DPR): cap 1.0 on limited-hardware class (2015 MacBook Air),
  1.5 on touch class (Pixel 6 Pro). Staged core path now installs the
  viewport resize handler (it previously had none).
- Canvas is never hidden/collapsed while renderer init is pending
  (removed #AwtsmoosCanvas from the pre-gameplay visibility:hidden rule).
- ONE boot state machine owns bootStage, runtimeState, and the loader veil:
  ready is refused while starting or failed; failed is terminal.
- Frame-budget plumbing: long-task monitor wired into the runtime loop;
  runtime.frameBudgetVerdict() exposes p95 vs 16.7ms and long tasks vs 50ms.
- Task 2 slice included in same commit: canonical chossid.glb fetch starts
  in parallel with renderer/terrain work; stage-specific deadlines
  (10s/15s/15s/30s/10s) replace the fixed 30s wait; five-proof loader stays
  until the machine reaches ready; no generated humanoid; heavy systems
  stay behind post-playable activation. First-control entry bundle remains
  7792 bytes (under the 8KB covenant); all chunks rebuilt deterministically.

Verification evidence:
- 110/110 app unit tests pass, 5/5 launcher tests pass, 9/9 performance
  tests pass, 10/10 new state-machine/gate tests pass (incl. fail-closed
  before timer starts, ready-refused-while-starting, failed-is-terminal).
- Build: deterministic chunk rebuilds verified; CSS validator shows zero
  NEW issues vs HEAD (100 errors / 591 warnings pre-existing, unchanged).
- Pre-existing failures NOT caused by this change: essential-grass.jpg
  untracked/missing (download 404s), index.html preload ?v= query test.

NOT deployed: left for Yaakov's review per the task's confidence clause —
the signed HTTPS deploy path is blocked (deploy key wiped from production
per 2026-10-09; /packed/deploy/status unreachable) and real-hardware
